    "leverage": {
      "desktop": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 800 480\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"nv3-leverage-en-desktop-title nv3-leverage-en-desktop-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-kind=\"leverage\" data-variant=\"desktop\"><title id=\"nv3-leverage-en-desktop-title\">Washington: licences and public equity</title><desc id=\"nv3-leverage-en-desktop-desc\">Two routes for government action. Licensing approves or restricts transactions; an equity investment requires authority, funds, an agreement over shares and defined rights. The Intel precedent is dated 22 August 2025: an announced $8.9 billion investment for 9.9% ownership, passive and without a board seat. The dotted Nvidia branch is an analytical scenario; the cited sources establish no government equity transaction in Nvidia. The diagram is qualitative; its dimensions do not measure financial amounts.</desc><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"798\" height=\"478\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\" stroke=\"var(--color-line-strong)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"35\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia Investigation\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\">Washington: licences and public equity</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"63\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia Investigation\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-muted)\">Regulatory powers and an equity transaction</text><path d=\"M376 95L400 81L424 95Z M378 101H422 M383 101V120M394 101V120M406 101V120M417 101V120 M378 121H422 M375 128H425\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-paper)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"151\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia Investigation\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\">Washington</text><path d=\"M364 105H200V143\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-signal)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round